//============================================================================
// nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads --- Calibre BOND PAD (BND) wrapper deck  (PROJECT-OWNED)
//
// Run it with:   DRC_GDS=/abs/path.gds scripts/calibre/run_bnd.sh
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// --------------------
// The Europractice mini@sic manual requires the final GDS to be "DRC/ANT/BND
// clean". BND is the wire-bond pad rule set and it has never been run on this
// design. Foundry deck:
//   /tsmc65pdk/65/CMOS/LP/pdk/Calibre/drc/wire_bond/CN65_WIRE_BOND_9M_6X1Z1U.20a
// -- 9M_6X1Z1U, an exact match to our metal stack. Same placeholder problem as
// the DRC and ANT decks (LAYOUT PATH/PRIMARY at deck lines 43-44, DRC RESULTS/
// SUMMARY at 46-47), so the same `DRC ICSTATION YES` wrapper pattern applies.
//
// TWO DECK SWITCHES MATTER HERE, AND BOTH ARE LEFT AS THE FOUNDRY SET THEM
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   #DEFINE with_AP   (deck line 33) -- "Turn on to use AP as the redistribution
//                     metal or metal Fuse after passivation". Our stack IS
//                     ...+AlRDL and the design has AP geometry, so leaving the
//                     foundry default is correct. If a run says otherwise,
//                     change it HERE, never in /tsmc65pdk.
//   #DEFINE SINGLE_PAD (deck lines 263,266) -- pad arrangement.
// If the broker's own switch set differs, theirs wins: ask before overriding.
//
// EXPECT NOISE ON THIS ONE, AND KNOW WHY
// --------------------------------------
// Bond pads (tpbn65v PAD70NU/PAD70GU) stream as near-empty black boxes -- 13
// polygons each, on 38/40, 39/60 and 74/0 -- and the passivation-opening layer
// CB (GDS 76) does not appear ANYWHERE in the stream. A bond-pad deck with no
// CB openings cannot evaluate pad-opening rules, so those will be silent rather
// than clean. The useful signal tonight is the metal/AP geometry around the pad
// ring, not the pad openings themselves. Treat a green CB result as absence of
// evidence, exactly as with the corner CSR checks.
//
// The foundry deck is READ-ONLY and is not copied, patched or sed-ed.
//============================================================================

DRC ICSTATION YES

LAYOUT PATH    "$DRC_GDS"
LAYOUT SYSTEM  GDSII
LAYOUT PRIMARY "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads"

DRC RESULTS DATABASE "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.bnd.results" ASCII
DRC SUMMARY REPORT   "nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.bnd.summary" REPLACE HIER
DRC CELL NAME YES CELL SPACE XFORM

DRC MAXIMUM RESULTS 1000
DRC MAXIMUM VERTEX  4096

#DEFINE LP

INCLUDE "/tsmc65pdk/65/CMOS/LP/pdk/Calibre/drc/wire_bond/CN65_WIRE_BOND_9M_6X1Z1U.20a"
